{"abstract":[{"text":"A partition of the elements ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<count"},{"text":" into disjoint sets, with union by size and path","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"halving. O(α(n)) amortized per operation.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/disjointsetmodule\/disjointset"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DisjointSet","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each set’s representative is one of its members. ","type":"text"},{"code":"union(a, b)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps the representative of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the larger set, or, for sets of the same size, the smaller of the two representatives, whatever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order of the arguments. Neither ","type":"text"},{"code":"find","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nor a union of elements already in one set changes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a representative, so representatives depend only on the sequence of unions that merged sets.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two disjoint sets are equal when they have the same elements, partitioned the same way. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representative "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"find"},{"type":"text","text":" returns is not part of the value: equal disjoint sets can name the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set by different representatives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","in